WEBVTT

00:01:29.990 --> 00:01:34.990
<b>First Ally</b>

00:01:36.530 --> 00:01:39.540
<i>Suigin, listen well.</i>

00:01:39.850 --> 00:01:42.330
Are you the one who kidnapped Riku Rei?

00:01:42.330 --> 00:01:43.460
Who are you?!

00:01:43.460 --> 00:01:46.110
If anything has happened to her, you'll pay!

00:01:46.650 --> 00:01:48.810
Calm down, Riku Suigin.

00:01:48.810 --> 00:01:51.250
You wouldn't be able 
to protect her right now.

00:01:51.640 --> 00:01:54.510
That's why we're keeping an eye on her.

00:01:54.510 --> 00:01:56.850
It was to protect her,

00:01:56.850 --> 00:02:00.100
but it's probably more interesting 
to call her a hostage.

00:02:00.100 --> 00:02:01.180
Quit messing with me!

00:02:02.720 --> 00:02:04.710
You want to save Riku Rei, don't you?

00:02:05.200 --> 00:02:06.980
Then, listen well, Riku Suigin.

00:02:07.300 --> 00:02:11.900
A certain festival will be held 
on stage 18 of <i>Grave Buster</i>.

00:02:12.650 --> 00:02:15.920
It's a festival for those who have
 cleared every stage in the game.

00:02:15.920 --> 00:02:19.570
It's also to prepare for 
conquering stage 0.

00:02:19.910 --> 00:02:22.710
In order for you to conquer stage 0,

00:02:22.710 --> 00:02:27.670
you'll have to head to stage 18 and 
find a player named Nishikaze.

00:02:27.670 --> 00:02:31.890
Nishikaze? How am I supposed to find 
a player I've never met before?

00:02:31.890 --> 00:02:33.800
You'll find out when you get there.

00:02:33.800 --> 00:02:35.560
I'll find out when I get there?

00:02:36.130 --> 00:02:38.590
What does this have to do with Riku Rei?!

00:02:38.850 --> 00:02:39.960
Hey, answer me!

00:02:41.480 --> 00:02:42.730
<b>Call Ended</b>

00:02:43.320 --> 00:02:46.860
Damn it. I'm left with even more questions.

00:02:51.620 --> 00:02:54.620
A mysterious lone wolf that doesn't speak.

00:02:54.610 --> 00:02:57.410
The no-charge meister who came from nowhere

00:02:57.410 --> 00:03:00.580
that defeats enemies with the 
lowest grade equipment... Gwin!

00:03:06.140 --> 00:03:09.960
Gwin! Gwin! Gwin!

00:03:09.960 --> 00:03:11.090
Gwin-san!

00:03:17.100 --> 00:03:21.610
I was cool in <i>Dungeon Century</i>, 
but I'm utterly useless right now.

00:03:24.590 --> 00:03:25.850
Wanchoi!

00:03:26.270 --> 00:03:28.770
I feel like I haven't seen you in forever.

00:03:45.270 --> 00:03:47.160
What are you looking at, Wanchoi?

00:03:50.040 --> 00:03:51.960
What's going on so early in the morning?

00:03:51.960 --> 00:03:54.670
Is there some kind of celebrity down there?

00:03:54.670 --> 00:03:58.460
You're so cute! Why don't 
you join our Cosplay Club?

00:03:58.460 --> 00:04:01.580
What school are you from? I don't 
think I've seen you here before.

00:04:01.580 --> 00:04:02.850
So cute.

00:04:03.310 --> 00:04:05.480
Flirting and bothering a girl like that...

00:04:05.480 --> 00:04:07.640
They really are trash normies.

00:04:08.110 --> 00:04:12.520
Can I get any of your SNS handles? 
Your email address? Come on, just tell me.

00:04:12.520 --> 00:04:14.090
I don't have any.

00:04:14.090 --> 00:04:15.690
What? No way!

00:04:15.690 --> 00:04:18.640
You don't have one in this day in age? 
Do you not talk to anyone?

00:04:19.830 --> 00:04:21.620
Riku Suigin!

00:04:21.620 --> 00:04:24.920
You said you'd save me, didn't you?

00:04:25.350 --> 00:04:27.020
Who's that?

00:04:26.050 --> 00:04:27.960
Gross! That nerd?

00:04:27.270 --> 00:04:28.500
That trash.

00:04:28.630 --> 00:04:29.780
Wh-What?

00:04:30.180 --> 00:04:32.160
Don't get in our way, stupid.

00:04:32.160 --> 00:04:33.020
So annoying!

00:04:33.020 --> 00:04:33.660
Loser.

00:04:33.660 --> 00:04:35.370
That's the guy who was cleaning the pool.

00:04:33.670 --> 00:04:35.460
What the heck's going on?

00:04:35.370 --> 00:04:36.890
The poor part-timer Suigin.

00:04:35.460 --> 00:04:36.970
Is today a bad day, or something?

00:04:36.890 --> 00:04:37.490
You bastard!

00:04:36.970 --> 00:04:38.970
Wanchoi, do you know what's going on?

00:04:37.490 --> 00:04:39.390
Don't get in our way!

00:04:39.390 --> 00:04:40.240
Get out of here!

00:04:40.240 --> 00:04:41.990
She's mine!

00:04:40.970 --> 00:04:42.330
Yeah...

00:04:42.670 --> 00:04:45.980
Huh? Could she possibly be Farin?

00:04:48.810 --> 00:04:51.520
Shinryou Academy 
Student Cafeteria

00:04:51.520 --> 00:04:53.650
<i>Uh, what's going on?</i>

00:04:53.650 --> 00:04:55.530
<i>Why'd she suddenly show up at my school?</i>

00:04:55.540 --> 00:04:57.500
<i>I'm not prepared for this at all.</i>

00:04:57.500 --> 00:04:59.750
<i>Not to mention she even brought a suitcase.</i>

00:04:59.750 --> 00:05:02.620
<i>Is she planning on staying in my dorm?</i>

00:05:03.110 --> 00:05:05.410
<i>What's with this awkward situation?</i>

00:05:05.410 --> 00:05:06.710
<i>What should I do?</i>

00:05:07.470 --> 00:05:08.690
Hey, Suigin.

00:05:08.690 --> 00:05:11.790
Huh? Oh, uh, how did you find me?

00:05:12.540 --> 00:05:16.130
Well, I work part-time as an instructor 
for the beginner's course,

00:05:16.130 --> 00:05:18.800
so I was able to find out 
some information about you.

00:05:19.110 --> 00:05:22.810
But, apparently, you really didn't 
want to see me, so I'm leaving.

00:05:22.810 --> 00:05:25.820
Huh? No way! 
Of course I'm glad you're here!

00:05:26.190 --> 00:05:29.850
<i>Aw, man... I actually 
got to see her, too...</i>

00:05:30.150 --> 00:05:33.320
<i>Now I really don't know what to say.</i>

00:05:35.040 --> 00:05:39.270
<i>Come to think of it, I'm a completely 
different person in game.</i>

00:05:46.430 --> 00:05:49.760
<i>I cause such a fuss in game,</i>

00:05:49.760 --> 00:05:54.660
<i>but in real life, I'm like the 
air that no one notices.</i>

00:05:55.240 --> 00:05:57.380
<i>My existence is completely empty.</i>

00:05:57.380 --> 00:06:01.950
<i>On the other hand, Farin stands out 
just like in the game.</i>

00:06:01.950 --> 00:06:04.430
Hey, isn't she cute?

00:06:04.430 --> 00:06:06.430
I think she's new. I wonder 
if she's a transfer student.

00:06:06.820 --> 00:06:11.890
<i>I wonder what she'll say, now that she 
knows how lame I am in real life.</i>

00:06:11.890 --> 00:06:13.120
Sir.

00:06:13.660 --> 00:06:16.110
You've been sitting here for an hour now.

00:06:16.110 --> 00:06:18.640
Are you going to order, or not?

00:06:18.640 --> 00:06:21.830
We have other students waiting.

00:06:21.830 --> 00:06:23.590
Is today a bad day?

00:06:23.590 --> 00:06:26.510
Damn it. They're too slow. I'm starving.

00:06:26.510 --> 00:06:30.070
Hey, isn't that the lame part-timer?

00:06:31.140 --> 00:06:32.400
Can I see the menu?

00:06:32.700 --> 00:06:34.890
May I get a menu, too?

00:06:34.890 --> 00:06:36.280
Here you go.

00:06:37.280 --> 00:06:39.090
Farin, what would you like?

00:06:39.360 --> 00:06:41.190
They all look so good.

00:06:41.190 --> 00:06:45.880
I'll have the avocado salad, minestrone soup,
 escargot, fried chicken wings,

00:06:43.760 --> 00:06:44.510
Avocado salad
Minestrone

00:06:44.510 --> 00:06:45.300
Minestrone
Escargot

00:06:45.300 --> 00:06:45.890
Escargot
Fried chicken wings

00:06:45.880 --> 00:06:48.460
teriyaki steak, squid tempura...

00:06:48.470 --> 00:06:49.930
<i>What the hell?</i>

00:06:49.930 --> 00:06:53.020
<i>She's so tiny. Is she the big eater type?</i>

00:06:53.020 --> 00:06:54.100
<i>Can she eat all of that?</i>

00:06:54.120 --> 00:06:57.800
<i>No, wait. The bigger question is 
who's going to pay for all of this?</i>

00:06:57.800 --> 00:06:59.410
<i>The only thing in my wallet...</i>

00:07:00.180 --> 00:07:02.350
<i>is a little bit of change.</i>

00:07:02.710 --> 00:07:05.930
<i>I'm not just poor. I am royally poor.</i>

00:07:06.280 --> 00:07:11.950
<i>All that money in the game is 
absolutely useless in real life.</i>

00:07:06.280 --> 00:07:12.200
<b>Saved Assets</b>

00:07:12.380 --> 00:07:16.470
Chilled ham pizza, 
cream pasta, special tiramisu...

00:07:16.470 --> 00:07:19.750
<i>Should we dine and dash? 
No, that's a crime. I can't...</i>

00:07:19.750 --> 00:07:21.670
And finally, this and this.

00:07:22.590 --> 00:07:25.550
Minestrone
Escargot
Fried chicken wings
Teriyaki steak
Squid tempura
Chilled ham pizza
Cream pasta
Special tiramisu
 Cheesecake
 Ice cream

00:07:26.220 --> 00:07:29.080
Okay sir, if you could pay now.

00:07:29.510 --> 00:07:32.720
You have to pay before you eat here.

00:07:32.720 --> 00:07:33.970
Oh, of course.

00:07:33.970 --> 00:07:37.400
<i>Wait, why did I just agree? 
I don't have that money!</i>

00:07:38.310 --> 00:07:42.230
Suigin, if that's not enough, 
you can order more.

00:07:42.230 --> 00:07:46.140
No, this is enough. I've been on a diet.

00:07:46.140 --> 00:07:47.690
<i>Not enough, my ass!</i>

00:07:47.700 --> 00:07:53.200
Teriyaki steak
Squid tempura
Chilled ham pizza
Cream pasta
Special tiramisu
 Cheesecake
 Ice cream

00:07:47.880 --> 00:07:49.910
Lunch is going to cost me 20,000?

00:07:49.910 --> 00:07:53.200
Well, if isn't the poor student Suigin.

00:07:53.200 --> 00:07:56.950
Why are you enjoying lunch at 
this expensive restaurant?

00:07:56.950 --> 00:07:59.760
You were going after 
Miss Riku Rei the other day,

00:07:59.760 --> 00:08:02.870
so did you change your mind
 after her dad died?

00:08:03.280 --> 00:08:06.900
This isn't a place for trash like you.

00:08:06.900 --> 00:08:08.580
Get the hell out.

00:08:08.580 --> 00:08:09.480
Hey.

00:08:10.260 --> 00:08:13.040
Don't talk to my leader like that.

00:08:13.040 --> 00:08:14.130
Leader?

00:08:14.130 --> 00:08:16.900
He's my leader in <i>Grave Buster</i>.

00:08:16.900 --> 00:08:18.800
He's a player worth over a hundred million.

00:08:18.800 --> 00:08:20.370
A hundred million?

00:08:22.090 --> 00:08:23.910
Just in <i>Grave Buster</i>...

00:08:26.460 --> 00:08:28.280
That's a hilarious joke.

00:08:28.280 --> 00:08:30.200
This little girl is hilarious.

00:08:30.200 --> 00:08:33.110
You shouldn't believe this guy.

00:08:33.940 --> 00:08:36.550
He's telling one lie after another 
because he wants money.

00:08:36.550 --> 00:08:37.440
It's not a lie.

00:08:37.440 --> 00:08:40.060
Oh? Then...

00:08:40.710 --> 00:08:45.050
Why don't you pay right now 
with your Shinryou coins?

00:08:45.050 --> 00:08:48.210
What? You can use Shinryou 
coins in real life?

00:08:48.650 --> 00:08:54.100
Yes. You can use Shinryou coins as 
well as other forms of e-money here.

00:08:54.100 --> 00:08:55.040
How?

00:08:55.360 --> 00:08:57.780
I just need to scan your Seabay.

00:08:58.480 --> 00:09:01.060
Hurry up and scan it.

00:09:01.060 --> 00:09:04.020
We'll prove this poor bastard's 
a con artist once and for all.

00:09:22.250 --> 00:09:23.340
<b>Payment complete</b>

00:09:23.340 --> 00:09:25.320
Thank you for your payment.

00:09:25.790 --> 00:09:27.110
No way!

00:09:27.110 --> 00:09:28.890
You sure your PDT isn't broken?!

00:09:28.890 --> 00:09:32.840
<i>Seriously?! You can use Shinryou 
coins as real-life currency?</i>

00:09:32.850 --> 00:09:34.470
This has never happened before.

00:09:34.470 --> 00:09:38.310
There are too many digits in the PDT 
that I can't get the exact amount.

00:09:38.930 --> 00:09:40.730
Gentleman!

00:09:41.360 --> 00:09:44.560
I told you so. He's a billion player.

00:09:51.690 --> 00:09:53.210
A girl student...

00:09:53.210 --> 00:09:54.770
Going into the guys' dorms...

00:09:56.740 --> 00:09:58.070
So cute...

00:09:58.070 --> 00:10:01.660
Damn him! I can't believe 
he's with such a cute girl!

00:09:59.770 --> 00:10:01.370
My heart!

00:10:00.840 --> 00:10:01.880
Objection!

00:10:01.660 --> 00:10:03.030
I'm going to report him!

00:10:03.040 --> 00:10:06.000
Hey, Suigin! Riku Rei-san's missing,

00:10:06.000 --> 00:10:07.840
and you've already got a new girlfriend?

00:10:07.840 --> 00:10:11.680
Shut up! I'm going to save 
Riku Rei, no matter what.

00:10:11.680 --> 00:10:13.340
You two-timer!

00:10:13.340 --> 00:10:14.600
Heartless bastard!

00:10:19.420 --> 00:10:22.640
Is the Riku Rei they keep talking 
about your girlfriend?

00:10:22.950 --> 00:10:25.580
No, she's not my girlfriend.

00:10:25.820 --> 00:10:28.650
Then what do you mean that 
you're going to save her?

00:10:28.860 --> 00:10:30.490
It's a long story...

00:10:30.900 --> 00:10:35.070
And telling you might 
put you in danger, as well.

00:10:35.410 --> 00:10:37.490
I can say this, though...

00:10:38.040 --> 00:10:40.500
Riku Rei is somewhere within <i>Grave Buster</i>.

00:10:40.860 --> 00:10:46.190
And no matter what, I'm going to 
find her and bring her back.

00:10:46.700 --> 00:10:50.200
That's why I'm really grateful 
that you joined my team—

00:10:50.200 --> 00:10:51.170
That's enough.

00:10:51.170 --> 00:10:51.940
Huh?

00:10:52.320 --> 00:10:55.840
Now that I'm on your team, 
you don't need to thank me.

00:10:56.200 --> 00:10:58.300
Let's go save Riku Rei-san.

00:11:00.010 --> 00:11:01.720
Let's log into <i>Grave Buster</i>.

00:11:12.810 --> 00:11:14.470
Isn't this...

00:11:15.130 --> 00:11:17.280
Why are there so many people here?

00:11:18.530 --> 00:11:21.130
Quit spacing out! 
The festival's about to start.

00:11:21.130 --> 00:11:22.110
Huh? Festival?

00:11:22.110 --> 00:11:23.680
Come on. Hurry up!

00:11:23.680 --> 00:11:24.930
S-Sure...

00:11:29.960 --> 00:11:34.970
<b>The Conquest Begins</b>

00:11:37.120 --> 00:11:41.210
Was this always a stage? 
It doesn't look like one.

00:11:41.210 --> 00:11:45.220
After a stage is cleared, 
it belongs to the players.

00:11:45.220 --> 00:11:51.950
Then they able to rebuild the buildings 
the way they want and level them up.

00:11:52.410 --> 00:11:55.600
This is now a place for players to gather.

00:11:56.020 --> 00:12:00.570
Come to think of it, the guy on the phone 
said there'd be a festival here today, too.

00:12:00.770 --> 00:12:02.900
Everyone knows about it.

00:12:02.900 --> 00:12:06.920
This festival is to prepare 
for conquering stage 0.

00:12:07.460 --> 00:12:12.860
The conquest of stage 0 is a huge event 
and there's no level limit for the players.

00:12:12.860 --> 00:12:14.060
Anyone can participate.

00:12:14.060 --> 00:12:20.050
That means there are top players here 
as well as newbies who want to try their luck.

00:12:20.470 --> 00:12:27.510
There are also players who just want to see 
what the mythical stage 0 looks like.

00:12:28.190 --> 00:12:29.940
Stage 0...

00:12:30.580 --> 00:12:33.450
<i>In order for you to conquer stage 0,</i>

00:12:33.450 --> 00:12:38.450
<i>you'll have to head to stage 18 and 
find a player named Nishikaze.</i>

00:12:38.450 --> 00:12:42.670
Nishikaze? How am I supposed to find 
a player I've never met before?

00:12:43.190 --> 00:12:45.040
<i>You'll find out when you get there.</i>

00:12:45.720 --> 00:12:49.300
Which means the Totems are also...

00:12:50.020 --> 00:12:54.580
Suigin, I don't know what your 
relationship is with the Totems,

00:12:54.580 --> 00:12:56.460
but they're really dangerous.

00:12:56.900 --> 00:12:58.760
I don't really know, either.

00:12:59.960 --> 00:13:03.020
He just keeps giving me information.

00:13:03.730 --> 00:13:07.080
And it seems that Riku Rei is with them.

00:13:07.800 --> 00:13:12.780
<i>I don't know how to find out how powerful 
their organization is or where they are.</i>

00:13:13.390 --> 00:13:15.980
You've never looked into 
information about the Totems?

00:13:16.340 --> 00:13:17.410
Information?

00:13:18.220 --> 00:13:19.060
Oh, yeah.

00:13:21.520 --> 00:13:26.050
Since she's the guide in this game, she 
might know something about the Totems.

00:13:27.100 --> 00:13:32.030
<i>Hello, Master! I've missed you! 
What can I help you with today?</i>

00:13:32.340 --> 00:13:35.570
So this is the kind of person 
you are, Riku Suigin.

00:13:35.570 --> 00:13:37.570
Don't get the wrong idea...

00:13:37.570 --> 00:13:40.380
She's... She's a very powerful tomb beast!

00:13:40.380 --> 00:13:43.710
<i>Are you going to do things to me again?</i>

00:13:43.710 --> 00:13:47.850
<i>I'm still completely worn 
out from last time.</i>

00:13:47.850 --> 00:13:49.700
Hey, what are you talking about?!

00:13:49.700 --> 00:13:50.810
People will get the wrong idea!

00:13:51.110 --> 00:13:53.770
<i>So, what are you going to 
make me do this time?</i>

00:13:54.000 --> 00:13:54.990
You perv!

00:13:54.990 --> 00:13:57.860
It's not what you think! 
We're just friends!

00:13:58.140 --> 00:14:02.060
<i>Friends? But you're my master, aren't you?</i>

00:14:02.060 --> 00:14:05.210
She's seriously a guide for the 
game that the system gave me!

00:14:05.210 --> 00:14:07.870
Go away! You big perv! 
I've lost all respect for you!

00:14:12.160 --> 00:14:14.340
Welcome. Please have a seat anywhere.

00:14:14.340 --> 00:14:17.400
Why are you a big eater in game, too?

00:14:17.400 --> 00:14:20.900
You're psychologically 
connected to the game.

00:14:20.900 --> 00:14:23.050
It's only natural to feel hungry.

00:14:23.300 --> 00:14:28.080
Not to mention, I lost a lot of HP 
due to your insensitivity.

00:14:29.410 --> 00:14:33.440
You wouldn't even let me talk and 
you hit me as hard as you could.

00:14:33.830 --> 00:14:36.870
Excuse me. Can I order? I'm starving!

00:14:39.820 --> 00:14:42.930
Hey, that's just instant ramen...

00:14:42.930 --> 00:14:45.570
Look at all the other delicious 
food in front of you.

00:14:45.960 --> 00:14:51.370
You have no idea how vital the existence 
of instant ramen is to poor students.

00:14:51.370 --> 00:14:53.420
Poor students?

00:14:53.420 --> 00:14:57.650
Come to think of it, I don't know 
exactly how much you have, but...

00:14:59.280 --> 00:15:00.580
What's wrong?

00:15:00.580 --> 00:15:03.730
Hey, did you hear? 
Another billion player appeared.

00:15:03.730 --> 00:15:07.070
Oh, come on. 
There are only five billion players.

00:15:07.070 --> 00:15:11.760
You're behind the times. Haven't you heard 
the rumors about a new billion player?

00:15:11.760 --> 00:15:15.850
Something about both Precious and Totems 
being attacked by this new player?

00:15:15.850 --> 00:15:19.270
Yeah I heard a number of higher-ranking 
players were defeated.

00:15:19.270 --> 00:15:20.230
Wow!

00:15:20.230 --> 00:15:21.650
Th-That's...

00:15:21.960 --> 00:15:23.910
Hey, he really showed up.

00:15:24.530 --> 00:15:25.740
Did something happen?

00:15:25.740 --> 00:15:27.620
<i>What should I do? 
It sounds like they know.</i>

00:15:27.620 --> 00:15:29.350
Should I just admit to it?

00:15:29.350 --> 00:15:32.210
I hoped people wouldn't find out,
 but that might not be possible...

00:15:32.850 --> 00:15:33.680
Let's go see!

00:15:33.680 --> 00:15:34.730
Hey, wait for me!

00:15:35.740 --> 00:15:40.580
Hey, what's up with those guys? 
I wonder if they found some amazing player.

00:15:41.190 --> 00:15:46.470
<i>I don't like being the center of attention, 
and that lifestyle doesn't suit me,</i>

00:15:46.780 --> 00:15:51.630
<i>but I guess it's only natural that I'd be 
noticed as the game's sixth billion player.</i>

00:15:53.720 --> 00:15:55.010
Move! I'm first!

00:15:55.010 --> 00:15:56.970
I'm the one who found him first!

00:15:56.970 --> 00:15:58.630
<i>I guess I can't keep it a secret.</i>

00:15:59.370 --> 00:16:02.450
Why are these people so worked up?

00:16:02.740 --> 00:16:06.440
Farin, there's something 
I need to tell you.

00:16:06.440 --> 00:16:08.360
Move! You're in the way!

00:16:08.360 --> 00:16:09.940
Out of the way, dumbass!

00:16:10.290 --> 00:16:12.150
What's the matter, Suigin?

00:16:12.830 --> 00:16:15.700
There's really nothing 
between Twin Star and me!

00:16:15.990 --> 00:16:17.850
Did you crack your head?

00:16:17.850 --> 00:16:19.090
Look! Over there!

00:16:19.090 --> 00:16:21.090
It sounds like something's happening outside.

00:16:24.350 --> 00:16:25.370
What is this?

00:16:25.950 --> 00:16:27.670
Flying penguins?

00:16:33.990 --> 00:16:36.750
Are we getting gifts because 
today's a festival?

00:16:36.750 --> 00:16:38.010
That's pretty fancy.

00:16:38.010 --> 00:16:39.350
They look like rings.

00:16:42.280 --> 00:16:43.640
What kind of rings are they?

00:16:45.350 --> 00:16:47.760
They're transfer rings to go to stage 18.

00:16:47.760 --> 00:16:50.950
That's where the last quest 
is to go to stage 0.

00:16:50.950 --> 00:16:54.020
Apparently the numbers are limited 
and it's first come, first served.

00:16:54.020 --> 00:16:56.710
I'm going to get there first!

00:17:01.090 --> 00:17:03.840
So this was the real reason 
behind the festival.

00:17:04.240 --> 00:17:06.860
The admins sure know what they're doing.

00:17:06.860 --> 00:17:09.380
At this rate, it looks like 
anyone can get a ring.

00:17:10.180 --> 00:17:14.000
What is the God Grave Tech Company 
actually trying to accomplish?

00:17:14.780 --> 00:17:17.970
If the administrators are 
transferring that many players,

00:17:17.970 --> 00:17:20.060
it's probably not just a festival.

00:17:20.630 --> 00:17:22.490
What are you going to do, Farin?

00:17:23.760 --> 00:17:26.150
If you're going to go, I'll go, too.

00:17:26.510 --> 00:17:28.680
All right. Let's go.

00:17:35.500 --> 00:17:39.280
Dark Tiger-sama, everything's 
going according to plan.

00:17:40.240 --> 00:17:44.200
All of the players are arriving
 with the transfer rings.

00:17:44.680 --> 00:17:51.050
Indeed, but this stage 18 
still has its guards and a boss.

00:17:51.050 --> 00:17:54.010
I've heard they are quite powerful.

00:17:55.930 --> 00:17:58.830
Let's have these weaklings act as meat shields.

00:18:07.810 --> 00:18:11.570
So this is the entrance 
to stage 0: stage 18.

00:18:14.540 --> 00:18:18.140
It doesn't appear to be a 
particularly dangerous stage.

00:18:18.790 --> 00:18:23.260
More importantly, how am I supposed to 
find Nishikaze among all these players?

00:18:24.160 --> 00:18:27.180
Aren't there any guards? 
That's inconceivable.

00:18:27.180 --> 00:18:30.930
You guys go ahead. I'll hide here 
and keep an eye on things.

00:18:34.270 --> 00:18:35.170
What's wrong?

00:18:36.380 --> 00:18:37.650
The guards appeared!

00:18:38.260 --> 00:18:41.600
Damn it! I didn't know there'd be 
this many tomb beast guards here!

00:18:41.820 --> 00:18:43.860
Whoa, why are there so many?

00:18:43.860 --> 00:18:47.760
So they basically need help 
from all the players.

00:18:48.270 --> 00:18:50.990
And things are just getting started.

00:18:57.910 --> 00:19:00.170
They have lots of different items.

00:19:01.780 --> 00:19:04.800
That's the portal to stage 0, right?

00:19:05.370 --> 00:19:06.740
Who are those two?

00:19:07.090 --> 00:19:10.450
I'm pretty sure that's 
Precious's leader, Dark Tiger.

00:19:10.870 --> 00:19:12.580
I didn't think he'd be here.

00:19:12.890 --> 00:19:16.420
<i>Dark Tiger... Another billion player.</i>

00:19:18.440 --> 00:19:21.690
It won't be good to have most of 
our meat shields killed by the small fry.

00:19:21.690 --> 00:19:22.890
Get rid of them.

00:19:23.210 --> 00:19:26.130
As you wish, Dark Tiger-sama.

00:19:26.130 --> 00:19:29.110
Let the festivities begin.

00:19:30.240 --> 00:19:31.410
Steel activate.

00:19:32.150 --> 00:19:34.070
Stallion Saber!

00:19:34.920 --> 00:19:37.020
Centurion Buster!

00:19:37.330 --> 00:19:39.610
Wh-What the heck is this?

00:19:45.040 --> 00:19:47.960
They defeated all the monsters 
on this stage in a single blow.

00:19:47.960 --> 00:19:50.620
This is Precious's power? That's insane.

00:19:51.000 --> 00:19:53.100
Bashida, it's time.

00:19:53.100 --> 00:20:00.170
Yes. Since the monsters have perished, 
I believe the boss will awaken.

00:20:02.340 --> 00:20:04.270
All the monsters disappeared!

00:20:04.270 --> 00:20:06.020
That means there's only the boss left.

00:20:06.020 --> 00:20:09.850
With all of these people here, we should 
be fine. We should be able to clear the stage.

00:20:12.640 --> 00:20:13.810
What the heck is this?!

00:20:14.080 --> 00:20:14.980
Is the boss here?

00:20:15.960 --> 00:20:17.140
Red water!

00:20:17.630 --> 00:20:20.950
No... It's not that the 
water's red. This is blood.

00:20:21.340 --> 00:20:23.900
Look! Something's inside the pool of blood!

00:20:23.900 --> 00:20:25.380
What the heck is that?

00:20:25.750 --> 00:20:28.200
That's the boss for this stage?

00:20:30.160 --> 00:20:33.580
Yes. The boss for stage 18... Aslan.

00:20:34.100 --> 00:20:37.630
Where is the blood that I seek?

00:20:37.630 --> 00:20:42.090
It looks really fun over 
there. I want to go.

00:20:42.090 --> 00:20:46.620
Nishikaze, Boss told us to wait here.

00:20:46.620 --> 00:20:48.580
Don't do anything you weren't told to do.

00:20:48.580 --> 00:20:50.070
I know.

00:20:50.690 --> 00:20:53.140
But I hate waiting.

00:20:53.140 --> 00:20:54.780
I'm going to go greet them myself.

00:20:57.610 --> 00:20:59.980
Full power unleashed! 
Let's take him down in a single volley!

00:21:01.900 --> 00:21:04.420
Magic mirror, Magic mirror, tell me...

00:21:04.420 --> 00:21:06.620
Where is the last tomb guardian?

00:21:06.950 --> 00:21:09.740
Look! His HP gauge hasn't gone down at all!

00:21:09.740 --> 00:21:12.590
His arm's shattered! 
Why isn't any damage showing up?

00:21:14.460 --> 00:21:19.720
That's amazing... He's using the pool 
of blood to regenerate his arm.

00:21:22.690 --> 00:21:24.590
So you're Riku Suigin?

00:21:25.020 --> 00:21:25.790
Huh?

00:21:26.850 --> 00:21:27.980
Huh?!

00:23:29.930 --> 00:23:33.940
<b>Next Time
Aslan's Trial / The Final Countdown</b>

00:23:30.320 --> 00:23:31.770
The Silver Guardian!
